To find the value of $\greenD{x}$, subtract $\dfrac{2}{3}$ from both sides of the equation:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{2} \goldE{-\dfrac{2}{3}}&=\greenD{x} \goldE{+\dfrac{2}{3}} \goldE{-\dfrac{2}{3}}\\\\
\greenD{\dfrac{4}{3}}&= \greenD{x}
\end{align}$

To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$ and $\goldE{\text{add } \dfrac{2}{3}} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{\dfrac{8}{3}}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{y} &= \greenD{\dfrac{8}{3}} \goldE{+\dfrac{2}{3}} \\\\
\maroonD{y} &= \maroonD{\dfrac{10}{3}}
\end{align}$
